{
  "requirement": "Number of hexadecimal digits in the identity hash of an anonymous selector segment.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub const HASH_DIGITS: usize = 12;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.outlines.HASH_DIGITS` declares one public constant, `pub const HASH_DIGITS: usize = 12`. It is the number of hex digits in the identity hash of an anonymous selector segment.\n\n- **Constant value.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs#fn[unknown_extensions_keep_nonblank_lines_and_content_selectors]` imports `HASH_DIGITS` from `outline::selector` and asserts `assert_eq!(HASH_DIGITS, 12)`. That assertion fails if the value changes.\n- **Digit count in real anonymous segments.** The same test checks every anonymous `line@…` selector that plain-text outlining produces.\n  - The prefix after `line@` has length `HASH_DIGITS`.\n  - Every character of the prefix is an ASCII hex digit.\n  - The prefix equals the first 12 characters of `structural_hash`.\n  - Equal lines get equal selectors and different lines get different ones.\n  - `select` resolves a selector back to its content.\n- **Other anonymous segments.** The tree-sitter and markdown outlines also build anonymous segments from `HASH_DIGITS`. They use the same single constant, which has no conditional or transformation, so the constant assertion and the plain-text check cover the obligation. The requirement states no further behavior for those paths.\n- **Marking.** The test carries a `{test}` reference to the requirement. `public_exports_match_the_appendix` also carries one and checks that the constant is part of the public API.\n\nI found no gap.",
